ond Sultan of Malwa, reigning from 1406 to 1435, son of the dynasty's founder Dilawar Khan Ghuri.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hoshea"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hoshea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hoshea</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hoshea was the last king of Israel, reigning from about 732 to 722 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hoshiarpur-district"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hoshiarpur-district.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hoshiarpur district</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Hoshiarpur district lies in the Indian state of Punjab, between the Beas and the Sutlej at the foot of the Shivalik hills, with its headquarters at the city of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hoshina-masayuki"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hoshina-masayuki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hoshina Masayuki</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hoshina Masayuki was a son of the shogun Tokugawa Hidetada and half-brother of Iemitsu, raised in the Hoshina family.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hosni-mubarak"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hosni-mubarak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hosni Mubarak</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hosni Mubarak was an Egyptian air force commander who became vice-president and, after Anwar Sadat's assassination in 1981, president of Egypt.</span></a></li></ul>
